SUMMARY:[Cantor Arts] Public Tour |  Auguste Rodin
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T123000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53694822395653-53694860283922@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a tour of our indoor and outdoor Rodin Sculptures!
  Our collection spans three galleries\, an outdoor sculpture garden\, and 
 features nearly 100 Rodin sculptures essential to telling his story and re
 presenting his groundbreaking engagement with the body.\n\nIMAGE: Auguste 
 Rodin (France\, 1840–1917)\, The Age of Bronze (L’Âge d’airain)\, 1
 875-1876. Bronze\, cast c. 1920. Gift of the B. Gerald Cantor Collection\,
  1983.300\n\nPublic Tours: Fridays and Saturdays at 11:30am \n\nAdmission 
 Info\n\nTours do\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Art & Architecture Library / Stanford University Libraries] Summe
 r Escape at Bowes Library
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T170000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52951257804174-52951257857476@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Take a little detour with Summer Escape at Bowes — our annua
 l snapshot of what’s new at the Art & Architecture Library\, presented w
 ith a seaside breeze. The promotional image’s soft bands of light and fl
 owing lines inspired how we arranged the show: items grouped to suggest cu
 rrents and horizons so each visit feels like a short visual voyage. You’
 ll find newly acquired artist’s books\, photobooks\, pop-up books\, and 
 railroad cars (?) that speak to creative practice\, sustainability\, and s
 torytellin\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:McMurtry Building
END:VEVENT
