SUMMARY:[Stanford Web Services] Introduction to Stanford Sites
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T160000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53845580112307-53845580112308@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Stanford Web Services offers a free monthly onboarding session
  that lasts one hour. We will walk you through the terminology\, common si
 te-building tasks\, and resources for taking the next steps. It is not han
 ds-on training\, but you can follow along by reviewing the steps below on 
 your own site during the session.\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-
 04 09:46 PDT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Health Library] On Demand: Plant-Rich Snacks for Lasting
  Energy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260904T180000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53384636572476-53384636606293@local-events
DESCRIPTION:On Demand: Plant-rich snacks can help you feel energized and s
 atisfied throughout the day. In this video\, learn how to prepare two easy
 \, delicious\, plant-rich snacks! Stanford Registered Dietitian Leah Gropp
 o demonstrates how to make a flavorful tofu dip and tasty nutty energy bit
 es.\n\nDeveloped by Stanford Registered Dietitians with support from Stanf
 ord Health Care Clinical Nutrition and the Stanford Nutrition Research Gro
 up\, this video delivers practical\, evidence-based guidance straight to y
 o\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://healthlibrary.stanford.edu/video/plan
 t-powered.html#snacks\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
URL:https://healthlibrary.stanford.edu/video/plant-powered.html#snacks
END:VEVENT
